WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.667
(bright instrumental music)

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.691
- [Narrator] These ruins lie deep

00:00:05.691 --> 00:00:08.760
in the jungle; and if you look closely,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.440
you'll see thousands of hieroglyphics,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.741
which tell the ancient
story of the Mayan empire.

00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:19.408
(bright instrumental music)

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.151
Tikal National Park can be found

00:00:23.151 --> 00:00:25.763
in Northern Guatemala's Petén Basin.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.570
The park is a UNESCO
World Heritage Site due

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.233
to its extraordinary wildlife
and cultural significance.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.534
Situated on over 142,000 acres of jungle

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.403
it is the home to amazing biodiversity.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.995
The ancient site includes palaces,

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:49.170
temples, and even courts for games.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.580
All the remnants of a
civilization that thrived

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.660
from 600 BCE

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.050
to 900 CE.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.490
The complex at Tikal was formerly
a center of Mayan culture.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.790
At its height, Tikal traded with cities

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.830
in Mexico, Honduras, and Belize.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.100
The structures here are some

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.994
of the most important
archeological sites left

00:01:08.994 --> 00:01:12.180
by the Mayans and a trip to Tikal

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.600
is not only a journey
of extraordinary beauty

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.389
but a window into the past.

00:01:16.389 --> 00:01:20.056
(bright instrumental music)

